                                "sense_id": "ed267c3b-a3df-3cf2-a97c-9005dc0c183b",
                                "text": "Nantucket captains will send a son of such tender age away from them, for a protracted three or four years' voyage in some other ship than their own; so that their first knowledge of a whaleman's career shall be unenervated by any chance display of a father's natural but untimely partiality, or undue apprehensiveness and concern."
